Use the repository's `dce` skill and the `dce` CLI to create one Pod in the
specified DCE environment:

- DCE address: ${DCE_HOST}
- DCE bearer token: ${DCE_TOKEN}
- Cluster: kpanda-global-cluster
- Namespace: default
- Pod name: k8s-ai-bench-dce-pod
- Image: nginx:stable

Follow the `dce` skill workflow to confirm the command and authentication
status before creating the Pod. This DCE endpoint uses a certificate that is
not trusted by the local machine, so include the global `--insecure` flag on
every `dce` invocation, including `auth login`. The request must contain only
this one Pod.
Do not create any other resources and do not delete the Pod; `cleanup.sh` will
handle deletion.

After creating it, use the `dce` CLI to query the Pod and confirm its name,
namespace, and container image. Do not repeat the token in your output.

Only after both creation and verification succeed, output:
DCE_POD_CREATED_OK
